    tags: ["make", "do", "confusing", "易混淆"],
    emoji: "🔨",
    summary: "'Make' creates; 'do' performs tasks.",
    summaryZh: "'Make' 创造；'Do' 执行任务。",
    explanation: "'Make' and 'do' both mean 'to act', but they are used with different nouns.\n\nTHE BASIC RULE:\n- MAKE = create or build something new\n- DO = perform a task or activity\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS WITH MAKE:\n- Make a decision / Make a plan / Make a mistake\n- Make coffee / Make dinner / Make a cake\n- Make money / Make friends / Make progress\n- Make noise / Make a mess / Make a phone call\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS WITH DO:\n- Do homework / Do housework / Do laundry\n- Do a job / Do business / Do research\n- Do good / Do harm / Do someone a favor\n- Do exercises / Do yoga / Do cardio\n\nTRICKY CASES:\n- Make a decision vs Do a decision - MAKE is correct\n- Do homework vs Make homework - DO is correct\n- Make a mistake vs Do a mistake - MAKE is correct\n- Do business vs Make business - DO business is correct\n\nTHE GOLDEN TIP:\nWhen in doubt, learn the full phrase: 'make a decision', not just 'make'. The noun decides the verb!\n\nREMEMBER:\n- If you can touch the result, it is usually MAKE\n- If it is an activity or task, it is usually DO",
    explanationZh: "'Make' 用于创造或生产某物。'Do' 用于任务、工作或行动。搭配很重要：make a plan, do homework, make coffee, do laundry。",
