    summaryZh: "掌握表示时间的 in, on, at。",
    explanation: "Prepositions are small words that show WHERE or WHEN something happens. The most common ones are: in, on, at.\n\nThink of prepositions like a map. They tell you the position of something in space or time.\n\nWHAT IS A POINT?\nA point is a tiny, exact location. Like a dot on a piece of paper.\n- Examples: 5:00, the corner, the station\n- Preposition: AT\n\nWHAT IS A LINE OR SURFACE?\nA line is flat and goes on. A surface is the top of something.\n- Examples: Monday, the table, the wall\n- Preposition: ON\n\nWHAT IS AN AREA OR ENCLOSED SPACE?\nAn area is a bigger space that surrounds something. Like a box or a room.\n- Examples: China, July, the morning\n- Preposition: IN\n\nTHE MAGIC RULE:\nThink SMALL -> MEDIUM -> BIG\n- SMALL (a point) -> AT\n- MEDIUM (a line/surface) -> ON\n- BIG (an area) -> IN\n\nTIME EXAMPLES:\n- AT 5:00 (an exact time point)\n- ON Monday (a day is like a line on the calendar)\n- IN July (a month is a bigger area)\n\nPLACE EXAMPLES:\n- AT the park (a specific point)\n- ON the table (a surface)\n- IN the box (an enclosed space)\n\nTRANSPORT RULES (very important!):\n- ON the bus, ON the train, ON the plane, ON the bike\n- IN the car, IN the taxi\n- AT the airport, AT the station\n\nWhy? Because a bus is big and you sit ON it. A car is smaller and you sit IN it.\n\nCOMMON MISTAKES:\n- in Monday - WRONG! Days use ON. ON Monday.\n- at China - WRONG! Big places use IN. IN China.\n- on 5:00 - WRONG! Exact times use AT. AT 5:00.\n\nMEMORY TIP:\nMake a small drawing of a calendar. Color the points (times) with AT-color, the lines (days) with ON-color, and the areas (months) with IN-color.",
    explanationZh: "'At' 用于具体时刻和节日。'On' 用于天和日期。'In' 用于月份、年份、季节和较长时间段。周末特殊：'at the weekend'（英式），'on the weekend'（美式）。",
